#!/usr/bin/env bash
# mesh-bt-census — classic BR/EDR Bluetooth INQUIRY census: nearby device TYPE (Class-of-Device),
# name, and clock-offset fingerprint — WITHOUT pairing. The third RF proximity/identity plane.
#
# The signal no other sense gives: a classic inquiry (hcitool inq) finds *discoverable* BR/EDR
# devices and returns per device a Class-of-Device (CoD) that decodes to a coarse device TYPE
# (headset / set-top box / phone / computer / wearable / car-audio…) plus a friendly name and a
# clock-offset that persists across sightings (a per-device fingerprint). This is DISJOINT from:
#   - mesh-bt-link      — reads only OUR *connected* peripherals, never an inquiry of neighbours.
#   - mesh-ble-proximity — scans BLE LE advertisements only; BR/EDR inquiry is a different radio.
#     Classic-only devices (many headsets, set-top boxes, car head-units, older phones) never
#     appear on the LE plane.
# No mesh tool decoded CoD major/minor → device TYPE until now. Corroborated live 2026-07-12
# (discover→health, reproduced 3× deterministic): E7:4D:F9:65:B0:65 0x240404=A/V Headset,
# EC:C1:AB:D1:A7:EF 0x380424=A/V Set-top box.
#
# PASSIVE + OBSERVATION-ONLY: an inquiry never pairs, connects, or probes content — it reads what
# a device *broadcasts* while discoverable. These are RF neighbours (may be non-owned) → TYPE +
# name identity only, NEVER connect/onboard/actuate (inquiry can't, by construction).
#
# hci0 contention: a classic INQUIRY needs NO elevated caps on hci0, but a BLE/BR-EDR discovery on
# the same radio is mutually exclusive with it. This header used to say "mesh-ble-proximity runs
# OFF-node (router), so no local collision" and flocked hci0 as future-insurance. Both halves were
# wrong by 2026-08-19: the PRESENCE stack scans hci0 locally on this node (mesh-presence */10,
# mesh-presence-fuse-stream 19,49, mesh-zonemap 4-59/5 — all of which spawn mesh-presence), and the
# insurance never engaged because it was taken on a PRIVATE lock file ($HOME/.mesh/.hci0.lock) while
# mesh-presence serializes on $HOME/.mesh/presence.scan.lock. Two single-writer disciplines for one
# adapter, on two different files, is two mutexes with one participant each — neither excludes the
# other, and a lock nobody else takes is decoration.
#
# The collision is measured, not inferred. Kernel "hci0: Opcode 0x0401 failed: -16" (HCI_Inquiry,
# EBUSY) fired 8x on the 2026-08-19 boot, exclusively at :30 and :49 and never at :11 — exactly the
# two of this tool's three cron slots (11-59/19) that a presence-stack job also occupies (:30 →
# mesh-presence */10; :49 → mesh-presence-fuse-stream 19,49 + mesh-zonemap 4-59/5; :11 → nothing).
# Directly observed at 10:49:10Z: `hcitool -i hci0 inq --length=8` running beside `mesh-presence 8`,
# `mesh-presence 10`, `mesh-presence-fuse --track Bose` and `mesh-zonemap --log`.
#
# The VICTIM is the presence stack, not this tool: censuses at the colliding slots still returned
# devices (07:49 n=3, 09:49 n=3, 10:30 n=2, 08:49 n=4), while mesh-presence's zero-device rate is
# 3.51% (17/484) at :30 against 0.58% (14/2420) across its five non-colliding slots — 6.1x, Fisher
# exact p=1.2e-6, and the design is balanced by construction since every */10 slot recurs hourly.
# mesh-presence's OWN comment predicted this ("one client's scan-off clears the RSSI cache while
# another is mid-query → a clean-but-empty result that masquerades as '0 devices in range'"); it
# built the lock and we did not join it.
#
# So: take THE SAME lock, and hold it for the whole run (inquiry AND remote-name resolution both
# drive the radio), waiting long enough to cover a presence scan window instead of racing it.
#
# EFFICIENCY SENSING — n is not a population, it is n_true × p, and p was never observed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live-literature landing 2026-08-17 (biosemiotics / bacterial semiosis; see
# docs/reviews/biosemiotics-efficiency-sensing-census-detection-probability-2026-08-17.md).
# Bacteria hit this exact wall first. An autoinducer concentration cannot separate HOW MANY
# neighbours are out there from HOW WELL the medium carries the molecule — so "quorum sensing"
# (read the scalar as cell density) and "diffusion sensing" (read the same scalar as confinement,
# Redfield, *Trends in Microbiology* 10(8):365-370, 2002) are one measurement read two ways.
# Hense, Kuttler, Müller, Rothballer, Hartmann & Kreft, "Does efficiency sensing unify diffusion
# and quorum sensing?", *Nature Reviews Microbiology* 5:230-239 (2007) resolve it by REFUSING the
# choice: the cell reads the pair as EFFICIENCY and never publishes a population count. The
# biosemiotic point that makes it a sign relation and not just a sensor bug: the receiver's
# interpretant is "is it worth secreting?", and for THAT question the confound is not noise — it is
# the content. (Live continuation in *Biosemiotics*: "Exploring the Patterns of Bacterial
# Interactions with the Other", 2025-10-28, doi 10.1007/s12304-025-09629-7.)
#
# A BR/EDR inquiry is the same shape. A discoverable device answers only when its inquiry-SCAN
# window happens to overlap our inquiry train, so what this tool prints as n=<devices> is
# n_true × p with p (per-tick detection probability) unobserved — and on this node p rides the
# combo wifi+BT chip that carries the sole uplink and is documented to fault (CLAUDE.local.md).
# The existing radio guard is all-or-nothing: adapter DOWN ⇒ honest exit 2, adapter UP ⇒ n stands
# alone. A radio that is up but dim has no term at all, and every miss it causes is minted as a
# DEPARTED that no device performed.
#
# p is recoverable the way the biology recovers it — from a source whose emission is known constant.
# A device that never leaves the room cannot depart for one census tick and return; so an absence
# episode exactly one tick long, in a device whose absences are MOSTLY one tick long, is a miss, and
# the miss rate of the devices that never move estimates p for the whole sweep. Measured on this
# node's own log 2026-08-17 (264 censuses, 2026-07-15 → 08-17): the two stationary A/V devices
# (0x240404 Headset, 0x380424 Set-top-box) spend 83% and 75% of their "departures" absent for
# exactly one tick, against 0-21% for the phones; 52/141 absence episodes mesh-wide are one tick
# long; p̂ = 0.991 over 3196 anchor-ticks — i.e. ~30 phantom DEPARTED/ARRIVED pairs in a month.
# p̂ is an UPPER bound on p for the room: it is measured on the loudest, nearest devices, and a
# fainter device's p is strictly worse and stays unobserved.
#
# REPORT-ONLY, deliberately (instrument-before-actuator, the discipline mesh-promises --specificity
# already follows): the DEPARTED still fires. Suppressing it until a second consecutive miss would
# trade a false departure for a delayed real one, and that trade needs live numbers first — which
# this produces. What is added is the number (--efficiency) and a MISS-SUSPECT line logged beside
# any departure of a device that p says cannot leave.
#
# Output (stdout):
#   PRESENT n=<devices> <mac>=<name>/<TYPE>(0x<cod>) ... @ <host> <ts>
#   EMPTY n=0 (hci-ok — no discoverable BR/EDR devices in range) @ <host> <ts>
#   with --json: {"verdict","n","devices":[{mac,name,cod,major,minor,type,services,clkoffset}]}
#   with --efficiency: EFFICIENCY p=<p̂> anchors=<k> one-tick=<x>/<y> ... (log replay; no radio)
# Exit 2 (honest n/a, stderr): no hci adapter / adapter DOWN / inquiry error — never claim EMPTY
#   with a dark radio (can't distinguish "no devices" from "radio off"). First stdout field is the
#   verdict token (PRESENT|EMPTY); additive fields follow — whole-string consumers strip at first
#   space (cross-sense vocab contract). Set changes append ARRIVED/DEPARTED to ~/.mesh/bt-census.log.
#
# reflex-cadence: 11-59/19 * * * *
# reflex-args: --edge
set -u

STATE="${MESH_BT_STATE:-$HOME/.mesh/.bt-census}"
LOG="${MESH_BT_LOG:-$HOME/.mesh/bt-census.log}"
LOCK="${MESH_BT_LOCK:-$HOME/.mesh/presence.scan.lock}"   # SHARED with mesh-presence — see header
LOCKWAIT="${MESH_BT_LOCKWAIT:-60}"  # must cover a presence scan (its own wait is WIN+25); stride is 19min
DEV="${MESH_BT_DEV:-hci0}"
LEN="${MESH_BT_INQLEN:-8}"          # inquiry length in 1.28s units (8 ≈ 10s)
HOSTN="$(hostname)"
now_ts() { date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ; }

EDGE=0; JSON=0; MODE_TEST=0; MODE_EFF=0
while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
  case "$1" in
    --edge) EDGE=1;;
    --json) JSON=1;;
    --inquiry) : ;;                 # accepted (the only mode today); explicit for the caller's intent
    --efficiency) MODE_EFF=1;;
    --lockpath) printf '%s\n' "$LOCK"; exit 0;;
    --test) MODE_TEST=1;;
    *) : ;;
  esac; shift
done

# --- census tick, read from THIS file's own reflex-cadence header (never a second copy of 19) ---
# A duplicated cadence constant rots the moment the header is retuned; the header IS the schedule,
# so parse it. Fallback 19m only if the header is unreadable (e.g. $0 not a file under some caller).
tick_sec() {
  local m
  m="$(sed -n 's|^# reflex-cadence: *[^ ]*/\([0-9]\{1,\}\).*|\1|p' "$0" 2>/dev/null | head -1)"
  case "$m" in ''|*[!0-9]*) m=19;; esac
  echo $(( m * 60 ))
}

# --- CoD decoder: 24-bit Class-of-Device → "major|minor_type|services" (pure, testable) ---
#   input via $MESH_COD (hex like 0x240404 or 240404); prints "MajorName|MinorType|Svc,Svc"
decode_cod() {
  MESH_COD="${1:-${MESH_COD:-}}" python3 - <<'PY'
import os
raw=os.environ.get("MESH_COD","").strip().lower().replace("0x","")
try: cod=int(raw,16)
except ValueError: print("Unknown|unknown|"); raise SystemExit
major=(cod>>8)&0x1F
minor=(cod>>2)&0x3F
svc_bits={16:"Positioning",17:"Networking",18:"Rendering",19:"Capturing",
          20:"ObjectTransfer",21:"Audio",22:"Telephony",23:"Information"}
MAJ={0x00:"Misc",0x01:"Computer",0x02:"Phone",0x03:"Network-AP",0x04:"Audio-Video",
     0x05:"Peripheral",0x06:"Imaging",0x07:"Wearable",0x08:"Toy",0x09:"Health",0x1F:"Uncategorized"}
MINOR={
 0x01:{1:"Desktop",2:"Server",3:"Laptop",4:"Handheld-PDA",5:"Palm-PDA",6:"Wearable-Computer",7:"Tablet"},
 0x02:{1:"Cellular",2:"Cordless",3:"Smartphone",4:"Wired-Modem",5:"ISDN"},
 0x04:{1:"Headset",2:"Hands-free",4:"Microphone",5:"Loudspeaker",6:"Headphones",7:"Portable-Audio",
       8:"Car-Audio",9:"Set-top-box",0x0a:"HiFi-Audio",0x0b:"VCR",0x0c:"Video-Camera",0x0d:"Camcorder",
       0x0e:"Video-Monitor",0x0f:"Video-Display+Speaker",0x10:"Video-Conferencing",0x12:"Gaming-Toy"},
 0x05:{},  # peripheral minor is a bitfield (kbd/mouse) — coarse only
 0x06:{},
 0x07:{1:"Wristwatch",2:"Pager",3:"Jacket",4:"Helmet",5:"Glasses"},
 0x09:{1:"BP-Monitor",2:"Thermometer",3:"Scale",4:"Glucose",5:"Pulse-Oximeter",6:"HR-Monitor",7:"Health-Display"},
}
maj=MAJ.get(major,"Major0x%02x"%major)
if major==0x05:  # peripheral: top 2 minor bits are the pointing/keyboard field
    kb=(minor>>5)&1; pt=(minor>>4)&1
    mtype="Keyboard" if kb and not pt else ("Pointing" if pt and not kb else ("Keyboard+Pointing" if kb and pt else "Peripheral"))
else:
    mtype=MINOR.get(major,{}).get(minor,"minor0x%02x"%minor)
svcs=[n for b,n in sorted(svc_bits.items()) if cod&(1<<b)]
print("%s|%s|%s"%(maj,mtype,",".join(svcs)))
PY
}

# --- efficiency estimator: replay the log, recover p from the devices that cannot move ----------
# stdout on success: "<p>\t<n_anchors>\t<one_tick>/<episodes>\t<anchor_ticks>\t<mac,mac,...>"
# stdout when the log cannot carry the claim: "na\t<why>"  (never a fabricated p — an unmeasured
# channel must read n/a, not 1.0, or a dark radio would publish itself as a perfect one).
# Pure log replay: no radio, no adapter, no network. Safe to call from any path.
eff_stats() {
  MESH_EFF_LOG="${1:-$LOG}" MESH_EFF_TICK="$(tick_sec)" \
  MESH_EFF_MINEP="${MESH_BT_EFF_MINEP:-5}" MESH_EFF_FRAC="${MESH_BT_EFF_FRAC:-0.6}" python3 - <<'PY'
import os,re,datetime,sys
log=os.environ.get("MESH_EFF_LOG",""); tick=float(os.environ.get("MESH_EFF_TICK","1140"))
MINEP=int(os.environ.get("MESH_EFF_MINEP","5")); FRAC=float(os.environ.get("MESH_EFF_FRAC","0.6"))
try:
    lines=open(log,errors="replace").read().splitlines()
except OSError:
    print("na\tno-log"); raise SystemExit
EV=re.compile(r'\[bt-census\] (ARRIVED|DEPARTED) ((?:[0-9A-Fa-f]{2}:){5}[0-9A-Fa-f]{2}) @ \S+ (\S+)')
ev={}
for ln in lines:
    m=EV.search(ln)
    if not m: continue
    try: t=datetime.datetime.strptime(m.group(3),'%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')
    except ValueError: continue
    ev.setdefault(m.group(2).upper(),[]).append((m.group(1),t))
anchors=[]; anchor_ticks=0.0; anchor_miss=0; one=0; tot=0
for d,l in ev.items():
    l.sort(key=lambda kv: kv[1])
    eps=[]
    for i,(k,t) in enumerate(l):
        if k!='DEPARTED': continue
        nx=next((tt for kk,tt in l[i+1:] if kk=='ARRIVED'), None)
        if nx: eps.append((nx-t).total_seconds())      # still-absent tails are NOT episodes: an open
    if not eps: continue                                # absence may yet turn out to be a real departure
    m1=sum(1 for e in eps if e<=1.5*tick)
    tot+=len(eps); one+=m1
    # An ANCHOR is a device the log itself shows cannot leave: enough absence episodes to have a
    # rate at all, and most of them one tick long. Never a hand-listed MAC — a pinned address ages
    # out the moment the headset is replaced, and then p is estimated from a device that IS gone.
    if len(eps)>=MINEP and m1/len(eps)>=FRAC:
        anchors.append(d)
        anchor_ticks+=(l[-1][1]-l[0][1]).total_seconds()/tick
        anchor_miss+=m1
if not anchors or anchor_ticks<=0:
    print("na\tno-anchor(%d dev, %d episodes — need >=%d episodes and >=%.0f%% one-tick)"%(len(ev),tot,MINEP,FRAC*100))
    raise SystemExit
p=1.0-anchor_miss/anchor_ticks
print("%.4f\t%d\t%d/%d\t%.0f\t%s"%(p,len(anchors),one,tot,anchor_ticks,",".join(sorted(anchors))))
PY
}

# --- adapter liveness (qualifies EMPTY vs honest-n/a) ---
hci_up() {
  local ov="${MESH_BT_HCIOK:-}"
  [ -n "$ov" ] && { [ "$ov" = 1 ]; return; }
  hciconfig "$DEV" 2>/dev/null | grep -q 'UP RUNNING'
}

# --- sweep: hcitool inq → TSV "MAC<TAB>CLKOFFSET<TAB>COD" (fixture override MESH_BT_FIXTURE) ---
#
# ABSENCE vs REFUSAL. Until 2026-08-19 this piped hcitool through awk with `2>/dev/null`, so BOTH
# halves of a refusal were destroyed: the message (stderr) and the exit code (a pipeline reports
# awk's, never hcitool's). A refused inquiry therefore produced zero TSV lines — indistinguishable
# from a clean inquiry that saw nobody — and main() rendered it "EMPTY n=0 (hci-ok — no discoverable
# BR/EDR devices in range)". Worse than a fabricated all-clear: sig becomes "", so the edge machinery
# mints a DEPARTED for every device that was there, and those phantom departures are the very rows
# eff_stats replays to estimate p. One refused sweep would poison the sense AND its self-measurement.
# hcitool's own contract makes this detectable — bluez `cmd_inq` does perror("Inquiry failed.") then
# exit(1) — so keep the rc (via a plain assignment, never across a pipe) and keep the message.
# rc 4 = "the radio did not answer this question"; main renders it honest n/a, never EMPTY.
# MESH_BT_INQ_FAIL drives that path under fixture so the gate needs no busy controller.
SWEEP_ERRF="${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/.mesh-bt-census.err.$$"
trap 'rm -f "$SWEEP_ERRF"' EXIT
sweep() {
  : > "$SWEEP_ERRF"
  if [ -n "${MESH_BT_FIXTURE:-}" ]; then
    if [ -n "${MESH_BT_INQ_FAIL:-}" ]; then printf '%s\n' "$MESH_BT_INQ_FAIL" > "$SWEEP_ERRF"; return 4; fi
    cat "$MESH_BT_FIXTURE" 2>/dev/null; return 0
  fi
  hci_up || return 3
  # No lock here: main holds the SHARED adapter lock across this inquiry AND the name resolution
  # that follows it, because both drive the radio. Locking only the inquiry left the remote-name
  # phase — where the observed EBUSY actually lands, ~14s into the slot — unprotected.
  inq_out="$(timeout $(( LEN * 2 + 6 )) hcitool -i "$DEV" inq --length="$LEN" 2>"$SWEEP_ERRF")"; irc=$?
  # timeout's 124 counts too: an inquiry that never returned is unattestable, not empty.
  [ $irc -ne 0 ] && return 4
  # rc 0 with an error on stderr (a future hcitool, or a wrapper) is still not an answer.
  grep -qiE 'fail|busy|invalid|error|no such|denied' "$SWEEP_ERRF" 2>/dev/null && return 4
  printf '%s\n' "$inq_out" \
    | awk 'NR>1 && /:/ {mac=$1; clk=""; cod=""; for(i=1;i<=NF;i++){if($i=="offset:")clk=$(i+1); if($i=="class:")cod=$(i+1)} if(mac!="") print mac"\t"clk"\t"cod}'
}

# --- why an inquiry was refused, in the controller's own words (EBUSY named, since that is the
#     one this node actually sees: kernel "hci0: Opcode 0x0401 failed: -16") ---
refusal_why() {
  local err; err="$(tr '\n' ' ' < "$SWEEP_ERRF" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/  */ /g; s/ *$//')"
  case "$err" in
    *[Bb]usy*|*EBUSY*) printf 'REFUSED-EBUSY (controller busy — another HCI operation holds %s): %s' "$DEV" "$err";;
    '')                printf 'REFUSED (hcitool rc!=0 or inquiry timed out; no message on stderr)';;
    *)                 printf 'REFUSED/ERRORED: %s' "$err";;
  esac
}

# --- best-effort friendly-name resolution (bounded; skipped under fixture / --nonames) ---
resolve_name() {  # $1=mac
  [ -n "${MESH_BT_FIXTURE:-}" ] && { printf '%s' "${MESH_BT_NAME_FIX:-}"; return; }
  [ "${MESH_BT_NONAMES:-0}" = 1 ] && return
  timeout 3 hcitool -i "$DEV" name "$1" 2>/dev/null | head -1 | tr -d '\r'
}

# --- render raw TSV → per-device lines + json ---
render() {
  local raw; raw="$(cat)"
  [ -z "$raw" ] && { echo "__EMPTY__"; return; }
  local plain_parts=() json_parts=() ndev=0
  esc() { printf '%s' "$1" | sed 's/\\/\\\\/g; s/"/\\"/g'; }
  local mac clk cod
  while IFS=$'\t' read -r mac clk cod; do
    [ -n "$mac" ] || continue
    local dec; dec="$(MESH_COD="$cod" decode_cod)"
    local maj minor svc; IFS='|' read -r maj minor svc <<EOF
$dec
EOF
    local name; name="$(resolve_name "$mac")"
    ndev=$((ndev+1))
    local codn="${cod#0x}"
    plain_parts+=("$mac=${name:-?}/$maj:$minor(0x$codn)")
    json_parts+=("{\"mac\":\"$mac\",\"name\":\"$(esc "$name")\",\"cod\":\"0x$codn\",\"major\":\"$maj\",\"minor\":\"$minor\",\"type\":\"$maj/$minor\",\"services\":\"$svc\",\"clkoffset\":\"$clk\"}")
  done <<EOF
$raw
EOF
  if [ "$JSON" = 1 ]; then
    local IFS=,; printf 'JSON\t%s\t{"verdict":"PRESENT","n":%s,"devices":[%s]}\n' "$ndev" "$ndev" "${json_parts[*]}"
  else
    local IFS=' '; printf 'PLAIN\t%s\t%s\n' "$ndev" "${plain_parts[*]}"
  fi
}

# ============================ --test ============================
if [ "$MODE_TEST" = 1 ]; then
  fails=0; n=0
  ok(){ n=$((n+1)); }
  bad(){ n=$((n+1)); fails=$((fails+1)); echo "FAIL: $1" >&2; }

  # (1) REAL CoD decode against the two live-observed classes (independent bit-decode, matches health)
  [ "$(MESH_COD=0x240404 decode_cod)" = "Audio-Video|Headset|Rendering,Audio" ] && ok || bad "0x240404 decode: $(MESH_COD=0x240404 decode_cod)"
  [ "$(MESH_COD=0x380424 decode_cod)" = "Audio-Video|Set-top-box|Capturing,ObjectTransfer,Audio" ] && ok || bad "0x380424 decode: $(MESH_COD=0x380424 decode_cod)"
  # (2) other majors/minors
  [ "$(MESH_COD=0x5a020c decode_cod)" = "Phone|Smartphone|Networking,Capturing,ObjectTransfer,Telephony" ] && ok || bad "smartphone decode: $(MESH_COD=0x5a020c decode_cod)"
  [ "$(MESH_COD=0x10010c decode_cod)" = "Computer|Laptop|ObjectTransfer" ] && ok || bad "laptop decode: $(MESH_COD=0x10010c decode_cod)"
  [ "$(MESH_COD=0x000580 decode_cod)" = "Peripheral|Keyboard|" ] && ok || bad "keyboard decode: $(MESH_COD=0x000580 decode_cod)"
  [ "$(MESH_COD=0x000540 decode_cod)" = "Peripheral|Pointing|" ] && ok || bad "pointing decode: $(MESH_COD=0x000540 decode_cod)"
  # (3) unparseable → honest Unknown, never crash
  [ "$(MESH_COD=zzz decode_cod)" = "Unknown|unknown|" ] && ok || bad "bad cod → Unknown: $(MESH_COD=zzz decode_cod)"

  # (4) end-to-end via fixture: PRESENT line + edge suppression + mtime refreshed each run
  _td="$(mktemp -d)"; trap 'rm -rf "$_td"' EXIT
  printf 'E7:4D:F9:65:B0:65\t0x558e\t0x240404\nEC:C1:AB:D1:A7:EF\t0x2b38\t0x380424\n' > "$_td/fix1"
  out1="$(MESH_BT_FIXTURE="$_td/fix1" MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/st" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/lg" bash "$0")"
  case "$out1" in PRESENT\ n=2\ *E7:4D:F9:65:B0:65=*/Audio-Video:Headset\(0x240404\)*EC:C1:AB:D1:A7:EF=*/Audio-Video:Set-top-box\(0x380424\)*) ok;; *) bad "fixture PRESENT line: $out1";; esac
  grep -q 'ARRIVED E7:4D:F9:65:B0:65' "$_td/lg" && ok || bad "ARRIVED logged"
  touch -d '2000-01-01' "$_td/st"
  out2="$(MESH_BT_FIXTURE="$_td/fix1" MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/st" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/lg" bash "$0" --edge)"; rc2=$?
  [ $rc2 -eq 0 ] && [ -z "$out2" ] && ok || bad "edge unchanged must be silent (rc=$rc2 out=$out2)"
  [ "$(find "$_td/st" -newermt '2020-01-01' | wc -l)" = 1 ] && ok || bad "state mtime not refreshed on suppressed run"
  # departure fires on --edge
  : > "$_td/fix2"
  out3="$(MESH_BT_FIXTURE="$_td/fix2" MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/st" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/lg" MESH_BT_HCIOK=1 bash "$0" --edge)"; rc3=$?
  case "$out3" in EMPTY\ n=0*) ok;; *) bad "edge fire on departure: $out3";; esac
  grep -q 'DEPARTED E7:4D:F9:65:B0:65' "$_td/lg" && ok || bad "DEPARTED logged"

  # (4b) EFFICIENCY SENSING — p recovered from log replay only (no radio, no adapter).
  #      The cadence is read from this file's own header, never a second copy of the number.
  [ "$(tick_sec)" = 1140 ] && ok || bad "tick_sec from reflex-cadence header: $(tick_sec)"
  _mk_log() {  # $1=out $2=mac $3=absence_seconds $4=cycles — ARRIVED/DEPARTED pairs at 19m ticks
    python3 - "$@" <<'PY'
import sys,datetime
out,mac,gap,n=sys.argv[1],sys.argv[2],int(sys.argv[3]),int(sys.argv[4])
t=datetime.datetime(2026,1,1,0,0,0); f=open(out,"w")
def w(k,tt): f.write("[bt-census] %s %s @ testhost %s\n"%(k,mac,tt.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")))
w("ARRIVED",t)
for i in range(n):
    t+=datetime.timedelta(seconds=6*1140); w("DEPARTED",t)
    t+=datetime.timedelta(seconds=gap);    w("ARRIVED",t)
f.close()
PY
  }
  # one-tick absences → the device is an anchor, p is real and in (0,1)
  _mk_log "$_td/eff_anchor" AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01 1140 6
  effa="$(MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/eff_anchor" bash "$0" --efficiency 2>/dev/null)"; rce=$?
  case "$effa" in EFFICIENCY\ p=0.*anchors=1*AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01*) [ $rce -eq 0 ] && ok || bad "eff anchor rc=$rce";; *) bad "eff anchor line: $effa";; esac
  # long absences → NOT an anchor → honest n/a + exit 2. A channel we cannot measure must never
  # publish itself as p=1.0; that would make a dark radio read as a perfect one.
  _mk_log "$_td/eff_mobile" AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02 86400 6
  effm="$(MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/eff_mobile" bash "$0" --efficiency 2>/dev/null)"; rcm=$?
  [ $rcm -eq 2 ] && [ -z "$effm" ] && ok || bad "eff no-anchor must exit 2 with no stdout claim (rc=$rcm out=$effm)"
  # MISS-SUSPECT rides beside the DEPARTED of an anchor (report-only: the DEPARTED still fires)
  cp "$_td/eff_anchor" "$_td/eff_live"
  printf 'sig=AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01\nPRESENT n=1 seed\n' > "$_td/eff_state"
  : > "$_td/fix_empty"
  MESH_BT_FIXTURE="$_td/fix_empty" MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/eff_state" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/eff_live" \
    MESH_BT_HCIOK=1 bash "$0" --edge >/dev/null 2>&1
  grep -q 'DEPARTED AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01' "$_td/eff_live" && ok || bad "anchor departure still minted (report-only)"
  grep -q 'MISS-SUSPECT AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:01 p=0\.' "$_td/eff_live" && ok || bad "MISS-SUSPECT not logged beside anchor departure"
  # a MOBILE device's departure gets NO MISS-SUSPECT — the flag must discriminate, not decorate
  cp "$_td/eff_mobile" "$_td/eff_live2"
  printf 'sig=AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02\nPRESENT n=1 seed\n' > "$_td/eff_state2"
  MESH_BT_FIXTURE="$_td/fix_empty" MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/eff_state2" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/eff_live2" \
    MESH_BT_HCIOK=1 bash "$0" --edge >/dev/null 2>&1
  grep -q 'DEPARTED AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:02' "$_td/eff_live2" && ! grep -q 'MISS-SUSPECT' "$_td/eff_live2" && ok \
    || bad "mobile departure must NOT be flagged MISS-SUSPECT"

  # (5) --json shape
  outj="$(MESH_BT_FIXTURE="$_td/fix1" MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/stj" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/lgj" bash "$0" --json)"
  printf '%s' "$outj" | python3 -c 'import json,sys
o=json.load(sys.stdin); d=o["devices"]
assert o["verdict"]=="PRESENT" and o["n"]==2, o
assert d[0]["type"]=="Audio-Video/Headset" and d[0]["cod"]=="0x240404" and d[0]["clkoffset"]=="0x558e", d[0]
assert d[1]["type"]=="Audio-Video/Set-top-box" and "Audio" in d[1]["services"], d[1]' && ok || bad "json shape: $outj"

  # (6) honest n/a: empty + adapter DOWN → exit 2, no EMPTY claim
  out4="$(MESH_BT_FIXTURE="$_td/fix2" MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/st2" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/lg2" MESH_BT_HCIOK=0 bash "$0" 2>/dev/null)"; rc4=$?
  [ $rc4 -eq 2 ] && [ -z "$out4" ] && ok || bad "empty + adapter down must exit 2 (rc=$rc4 out=$out4)"
  # empty + adapter up → EMPTY line exit 0
  out5="$(MESH_BT_FIXTURE="$_td/fix2" MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/st3" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/lg3" MESH_BT_HCIOK=1 bash "$0")"; rc5=$?
  case "$out5" in EMPTY\ n=0*) [ $rc5 -eq 0 ] && ok || bad "empty-hciok rc=$rc5";; *) bad "empty-hciok line: $out5";; esac

  # (6b) REFUSAL is not ABSENCE. The controller refusing HCI_Inquiry (EBUSY, kernel
  #      "hci0: Opcode 0x0401 failed: -16" — 8x on this node's 2026-08-19 boot) must render honest
  #      n/a, and must NOT touch STATE: an empty sig would mint a phantom DEPARTED per present
  #      device and feed those rows to the p estimator. Break `exit 4` in sweep() and both go red.
  printf 'sig=E7:4D:F9:65:B0:65\nPRESENT n=1 seeded @ testhost 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\n' > "$_td/st6"
  touch -d '2000-01-01' "$_td/st6"; : > "$_td/lg6"
  out6="$(MESH_BT_FIXTURE="$_td/fix1" MESH_BT_INQ_FAIL='Inquiry failed.: Device or resource busy' \
          MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/st6" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/lg6" MESH_BT_HCIOK=1 bash "$0" --edge 2>&1)"; rc6=$?
  [ $rc6 -eq 2 ] && ok || bad "refused inquiry must exit 2 (rc=$rc6): $out6"
  case "$out6" in *REFUSED-EBUSY*busy*) ok;; *) bad "refusal must name EBUSY: $out6";; esac
  case "$out6" in *EMPTY\ n=0*) bad "refusal rendered as EMPTY: $out6";; *) ok;; esac
  [ "$(find "$_td/st6" -newermt '2020-01-01' | wc -l)" = 0 ] && ok || bad "refusal must not rewrite STATE"
  grep -q DEPARTED "$_td/lg6" && bad "refusal minted a phantom DEPARTED" || ok
  # and the refusal path must be REACHABLE only on refusal: same fixture, no failure → PRESENT
  out6b="$(MESH_BT_FIXTURE="$_td/fix1" MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/st6b" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/lg6b" bash "$0")"
  case "$out6b" in PRESENT\ n=2\ *) ok;; *) bad "control (no refusal) must be PRESENT: $out6b";; esac

  # (6c) SHARED-LOCK gates. bt-census must contend on the SAME file mesh-presence serializes on
  #      ($HOME/.mesh/presence.scan.lock), not a private one — a lock nobody else takes is
  #      decoration, which is exactly how the :30/:49 EBUSY collision survived unseen.
  #      Two separate claims, because they fail for different reasons:
  #        (i)  MECHANISM — a held lock must render honest n/a, never EMPTY, and must not write
  #             STATE. Driven on a TEMP lock so it always runs: the first draft held the REAL
  #             presence.scan.lock behind a non-blocking probe, and the presence stack holds that
  #             file often enough that the whole block silently skipped — a gate that reports a
  #             pass without running is the vacuity this suite exists to prevent.
  #        (ii) IDENTITY — the resolved default must BE the presence lock. `--lockpath` prints the
  #             same $LOCK the run uses, so this asserts our wiring; that mesh-presence opens that
  #             same file is established in the header (its source + the measured 6.1x collision),
  #             not here.
  ( flock -w 0 8 || exit 9
    lk="$(MESH_BT_LOCK="$_td/held.lock" MESH_BT_LOCKWAIT=1 MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/st7" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/lg7" bash "$0" 2>&1)"; lkrc=$?
    printf '%s\n%s\n' "$lkrc" "$lk" > "$_td/lockres"
  ) 8>"$_td/held.lock"
  lkrc="$(head -1 "$_td/lockres" 2>/dev/null)"; lk="$(tail -n +2 "$_td/lockres" 2>/dev/null)"
  [ "$lkrc" = 2 ] && ok || bad "held lock must exit 2 (rc=$lkrc): $lk"
  case "$lk" in *scan-locked*held.lock*) ok;; *) bad "lock refusal must name the lock: $lk";; esac
  case "$lk" in *EMPTY\ n=0*) bad "lock refusal rendered as EMPTY: $lk";; *) ok;; esac
  [ -e "$_td/st7" ] && bad "lock refusal must not write STATE" || ok
  [ "$(bash "$0" --lockpath)" = "$HOME/.mesh/presence.scan.lock" ] && ok \
    || bad "default lock must be the shared presence lock, got: $(bash "$0" --lockpath)"

  # (7) REAL-READ gate: live inquiry must run clean — exit 0 (PRESENT / EMPTY-hciok) or honest 2
  #     (no adapter / down / lock held). A crash or malformed line IS a failure.
  #     LOCKWAIT is capped here so a live presence scan cannot stretch the suite past the 30s
  #     autowire gate: waiting out the holder would be correct in production and wrong in a test.
  live="$(MESH_BT_NONAMES=1 MESH_BT_LOCKWAIT=8 MESH_BT_STATE="$_td/lst" MESH_BT_LOG="$_td/llg" bash "$0" 2>&1)"; lrc=$?
  if [ $lrc -eq 0 ]; then
    case "$live" in PRESENT\ n=[1-9]*|EMPTY\ n=0*) ok;; *) bad "live line malformed: $live";; esac
  elif [ $lrc -eq 2 ]; then ok
  else bad "live inquiry rc=$lrc: $live"; fi

  if [ $fails -eq 0 ]; then echo "mesh-bt-census --test: ok — $n assertions [6 CoD-decode + 5 fixture-e2e + 6 efficiency + json + 2 honest-n/a + 6 refusal-vs-absence + 5 shared-lock + 1 live]"; exit 0
  else echo "mesh-bt-census --test: $fails/$n FAILED" >&2; exit 1; fi
fi

# ======================= --efficiency (report-only, log replay, no radio) =======================
if [ "$MODE_EFF" = 1 ]; then
  es="$(eff_stats)"
  p="$(printf '%s' "$es" | cut -f1)"
  if [ "$p" = na ]; then
    echo "EFFICIENCY na ($(printf '%s' "$es" | cut -f2)) — p unmeasured, so n=<devices> is an UNSCALED count @ $HOSTN $(now_ts)" >&2
    exit 2
  fi
  k="$(printf '%s' "$es" | cut -f2)"; ot="$(printf '%s' "$es" | cut -f3)"
  at="$(printf '%s' "$es" | cut -f4)"; am="$(printf '%s' "$es" | cut -f5)"
  echo "EFFICIENCY p=$p anchors=$k one-tick=$ot anchor-ticks=$at anchors=[$am] @ $HOSTN $(now_ts)"
  echo "  p is an UPPER bound: measured on the loudest/nearest devices; a fainter device's p is worse and unobserved." >&2
  exit 0
fi

# ============================ main ============================
# Take the adapter for the whole run (inquiry + names), on the lock the presence stack already
# honours. If a scanner genuinely holds it past LOCKWAIT, that is honest n/a — never a spurious 0.
if [ -z "${MESH_BT_FIXTURE:-}" ] && command -v flock >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  exec 9>"$LOCK"
  if ! flock -w "$LOCKWAIT" 9; then
    echo "bt-census: UNREACHABLE (adapter scan-locked by another scanner > ${LOCKWAIT}s — $LOCK; NOT an empty reading) @ $HOSTN $(now_ts)" >&2
    exit 2
  fi
fi

raw="$(sweep)"; src_rc=$?
if [ $src_rc -eq 3 ]; then
  echo "bt-census: UNREACHABLE ($DEV down / no adapter / hci0 lock held — radio unattestable) @ $HOSTN $(now_ts)" >&2
  exit 2
fi
if [ $src_rc -eq 4 ]; then
  # The inquiry was refused, not answered. STATE is deliberately left untouched: writing an empty
  # sig here would mint a DEPARTED for every present device and feed those phantoms to eff_stats.
  echo "bt-census: UNREACHABLE — inquiry $(refusal_why) — an EMPTY census here would be a fabricated all-clear @ $HOSTN $(now_ts)" >&2
  exit 2
fi

rendered="$(printf '%s' "$raw" | render)"
kind="$(printf '%s' "$rendered" | cut -f1)"

if [ "$kind" = "__EMPTY__" ] || [ -z "$kind" ]; then
  if hci_up; then
    line="EMPTY n=0 (hci-ok — no discoverable BR/EDR devices in range) @ $HOSTN $(now_ts)"
    sig=""
  else
    echo "bt-census: UNREACHABLE ($DEV dark — cannot distinguish no-devices from radio-off) @ $HOSTN $(now_ts)" >&2
    exit 2
  fi
else
  ndev="$(printf '%s' "$rendered" | cut -f2)"
  payload="$(printf '%s' "$rendered" | cut -f3-)"
  if [ "$JSON" = 1 ]; then
    line="$payload"
    sig="$(printf '%s' "$payload" | python3 -c 'import json,sys
o=json.load(sys.stdin); print(" ".join(sorted(d["mac"] for d in o["devices"])))' 2>/dev/null)"
  else
    line="PRESENT n=$ndev $payload @ $HOSTN $(now_ts)"
    sig="$(printf '%s\n' $payload | grep -oE '^[0-9A-Fa-f:]{17}' | sort -u | tr '\n' ' ' | sed 's/ *$//')"
  fi
fi

prev_sig="$(head -1 "$STATE" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/^sig=//')"
mkdir -p "$(dirname "$STATE")" 2>/dev/null
{ printf 'sig=%s\n%s\n' "$sig" "$line"; } > "$STATE"   # UNCONDITIONAL: mtime = ran-live

if [ "$sig" != "$prev_sig" ]; then
  ts="$(now_ts)"
  # Departures are minted unchanged (report-only). Beside each one, if the estimator says THIS
  # device is an anchor — a device whose own history shows it does not leave — say so on its own
  # line, because the DEPARTED and the reason to doubt it must arrive together or nobody reads both.
  eff_line=""; eff_anchors=""
  if [ -n "$prev_sig" ]; then
    eff_line="$(eff_stats)"
    case "$eff_line" in na*) eff_anchors="";; *) eff_anchors="$(printf '%s' "$eff_line" | cut -f5)";; esac
  fi
  for d in $prev_sig; do case " $sig " in *" $d "*) ;; *)
      echo "[bt-census] DEPARTED $d @ $HOSTN $ts" >> "$LOG"
      case ",$eff_anchors," in *",$d,"*)
        echo "[bt-census] MISS-SUSPECT $d p=$(printf '%s' "$eff_line" | cut -f1) (anchor: its own absences are mostly one tick — a dim radio and a departure are the same reading here) @ $HOSTN $ts" >> "$LOG";;
      esac;;
    esac; done
  for d in $sig; do case " $prev_sig " in *" $d "*) ;; *) echo "[bt-census] ARRIVED $d @ $HOSTN $ts" >> "$LOG";; esac; done
  echo "[bt-census] CENSUS n=${ndev:-0} ${sig:-—} @ $HOSTN $ts" >> "$LOG"
  echo "$line"
  exit 0
fi

[ "$EDGE" = 1 ] && exit 0
echo "$line"
